# Sanctum — .gitignore
# Secrets NEVER enter the repo (they live in a secrets manager). Runtime data is transient.
# NOTE: a .gitignore cannot catch an inline IP or secret pasted into a tracked file —
# any relay/VPN IP or credential must be scrubbed BY HAND from committed config.

# --- Credentials / tokens ---
rclone.conf
.env
.env.*
*.key
*.pem
*_token*
*token*.json
*credentials*.json
*service-account*.json
*service_account*.json
secrets/
.secrets/

# --- Runtime data (kept out of git; the corpus is NOT transient) ---
# The corpus is PERMANENT and lives in the corpus store. It is excluded here
# because it is large, not because it is disposable. Retention is load-bearing:
# core/lexicanum.py recomputes matches on demand instead of storing them, which
# is what lets a group invented today be run against everything collected last
# year. Pruning the corpus would silently destroy that, and would turn the
# vocabulary-granularity decision into a permanent one.
# Read VOCABULARY.md §4 before changing retention.
corpus/
seen.txt
seen_titles.txt
*.log
logs/*.log
staging_candidates.md

# --- Python cruft ---
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/

# --- OS / editor ---
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
.idea/
.vscode/

# --- Reference material: kept LOCAL, never published ---
# Working notes, feed candidate lists, and the effort briefing stay on your
# machine but are not committed (they carry internal/host detail).
*/references/
references/

# --- Legacy. The scrub check was removed 2026-08-23, but anyone who created a
# .scrub-denylist while it existed still has one on disk. The rule stays so that
# file can never be committed by accident. Do not delete this line to tidy up.
.scrub-denylist

# --- Second domain: kept out of the public repo entirely.
s2/
.githooks/

# Private: never publish
claude_S2-running-log.md
deploy-s2.ps1
deploy-*.ps1
